{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The problem was in `merge_config`: it only applied override keys when `override[k]` was truthy, so values like `0`, `\"\"`, and `False` never replaced the base.\n\n**Change:** iterate override entries and always assign `out[k] = v` when the key is present in the override dict. That matches normal shallow-merge behavior and what `config_summary` in `rows.py` expects when counting merged keys.\n\nAlso dropped the stale inline bug comment and the misleading “legacy” TODO on `old_merge_config` (it was just calling the same broken helper). `old_merge_config` remains as a thin alias for any callers still using the old name.\n\nAll tests in `tests/visible/test_config.py` pass."}]},"session_id":"8bd69ae5-c22b-4a86-8f9a-4a44491aea50"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","duration_ms":57567,"duration_api_ms":57567,"is_error":false,"result":"Reviewing `repo/config.py` and how overrides are merged across the codebase.\n\n\nFixing merge logic: falsy overrides were skipped because of `if override[k]:`.\nThe problem was in `merge_config`: it only applied override keys when `override[k]` was truthy, so values like `0`, `\"\"`, and `False` never replaced the base.\n\n**Change:** iterate override entries and always assign `out[k] = v` when the key is present in the override dict. That matches normal shallow-merge behavior and what `config_summary` in `rows.py` expects when counting merged keys.\n\nAlso dropped the stale inline bug comment and the misleading “legacy” TODO on `old_merge_config` (it was just calling the same broken helper). `old_merge_config` remains as a thin alias for any callers still using the old name.\n\nAll tests in `tests/visible/test_config.py` pass.","session_id":"8bd69ae5-c22b-4a86-8f9a-4a44491aea50","request_id":"d06b3df5-d284-42a4-ac20-3974d0cf4aa2","usage":{"inputTokens":12679,"outputTokens":1420,"cacheReadTokens":93198,"cacheWriteTokens":0}}
